course: dictionary
lesson: 2610
title: Depth: how far down something goes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Depth is how far something goes down from the top. Look at the words around it for clues. «tides change the depth, and hidden rocks or rubbish lie under the surface» tells you depth is about how far down the water goes, and what lies down there.
explain: Depth can also mean how far back something goes, like the depth of a shelf. The depths are the deepest parts, like the depths of the ocean. A word such as deep, down or under near the word depth is a clue that it means distance.
explain: «In depth» means in a full, careful way. «Out of your depth» means in water too deep for you, or in something too hard. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Depth is a measure of length, measured downward from the top.
fact: With length and width, depth gives volume: length × width × depth.
fact: «The UK minimum tread depth for cars is 1.6 millimetres.» Tread depth is the depth of the grooves in a tyre.
fact: «The depths of the ocean» means the deepest parts of the sea.
fact: Ship sonar measures depth by sending sound down and timing the echo.
exercise: In the sum length × width × depth, what does depth measure? | How heavy something is | *How far something goes down, from top to bottom | How many people can fit inside
exercise: Why does the text say to check the depth of water before you jump in? | *So you know how deep it is, and whether there are hidden rocks | So the water feels warmer | So you can see your reflection clearly
exercise: Ravi says, «I'm out of my depth in this maths test.» What does he mean? | He has finished the test early | *The work is too hard for him | He has swum into the deep sea
test: What helps a goldfish stay at one depth? | Cold water around it | Its long, bright tail | *The right amount of gas in its swim bladder
test: «Tombstoning» means jumping into water from piers, cliffs or bridges. What is one danger? | *Tides change the depth, and hidden rocks may lie under the surface | The water is always warm | Fish will bite your toes
exam: Ms Patel explained the plan «in depth». What does in depth mean here? | Far under the water | *In a full, careful way | Very quickly and loudly
